nvidia-compute-toggle is an independent implementation inspired by
donfreiday/nvidia-disable:

  https://github.com/donfreiday/nvidia-disable

It is not a git fork and does not include the upstream repository's history.
The upstream project documents the PCI remove/rescan + D3cold technique for
permanently disabling a faulty dGPU on the XPS 15 9570. This project applies the
same low-level technique to the opposite use case: keeping the dGPU available
for on-demand CUDA.

At the time of writing, the upstream repository has no LICENSE file, so its code
is under default copyright. This project's original code is MIT-licensed; it
does not relicense upstream code. If you want to copy code from the upstream
project, ask its author for permission or terms.

The technique itself (removing a PCI device and rescanning the bus) and standard
systemd unit patterns are not claimed as original.
